app/courses/[slug]/page.tsx after the fix (no export const dynamicParams anywhere in the route):

export async function generateStaticParams() {
  const slugs = await getPopularCourseSlugs(200);
  return slugs.map((slug) => ({ slug }));
}

export default async function CoursePage({ params }: { params: Promise<{ slug: string }> }) {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const course = await getCourse(slug);
  if (!course) notFound();
  return <CourseView course={course} />;
}

Build log: Generating static pages (214/214)
"sql-joins-in-practice" is course number 431 by views and exists in the API.

Statement: "A request for /courses/sql-joins-in-practice is rendered on demand when it first arrives instead of answering 404, because generateStaticParams only decides which pages are prerendered at build."

A reviewer proposes this change "so that bots cannot make us render random slugs":

// app/courses/[slug]/page.tsx
+export const dynamicParams = false;

 export async function generateStaticParams() {
   const slugs = await getPopularCourseSlugs(200);
   return slugs.map((slug) => ({ slug }));
 }

// lib/courses.ts (unchanged)
fetch(`https://api.codedev.test/v1/courses/${slug}`, { next: { revalidate: 3600, tags: [`course:${slug}`] } })

The day after the deploy, an instructor publishes the new course "rust-for-web-devs". No deploy follows.

Statement: "/courses/rust-for-web-devs will render on its first request and be cached for an hour, because its data fetch has revalidate: 3600 and a course tag."
